    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nWhen released from rest, mechanical energy is conserved: $mg x_m = \\frac{1}{2} k x_m^2 \\implies x_m = \\frac{2mg}{k}$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nMass $m = 1\\text{ kg}$, spring constant $k = 300\\text{ N/m}$, $g = 10\\text{ m/s}^2$.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nx_m = \\frac{2mg}{k}\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. At maximum extension x_m, mass momentarily stops so Delta K = 0.\n2. Loss in gravitational PE = Gain in spring PE: mg x_m = 0.5 k x_m^2.\n3. x_m = 2mg / k = (2 * 1 * 10) / 300 = 0.067 m.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 0.067 m\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nEquilibrium extension is mg/k, but maximum extension upon release from rest is exactly 2mg/k!",
